Title: Post-hoc validator for related-work-note — re-resolve DOIs and URLs
Status: open
Created: 2026-04-17
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-04-17T08:37Z claude created — spawned from ticket 0098 review. Skill 0098 specifies a DOI/URL resolution step before emission, but enforcement depends on the invoked model actually doing it. An external validator closes the gap.

--- body ---
## Context

The `related-work-note` skill (ticket 0098, installed at
`~/.claude/skills/related-work-note/SKILL.md`) instructs the invoked
model to `WebFetch` every DOI and URL before emitting the note, and
to drop or replace unresolved entries. This is a structural guard
against hallucinated citations, which LLMs are notorious for
producing in academic prose.

The gap: the skill *specifies* the check, but does not *enforce* it.
A model under load, or on a budget, or a model that misreads the
skill instructions, can skip the resolution step and still emit a
structurally valid note. The author verification checklist catches
the problem eventually — but only if the author bothers — and by
then the bad citation may already be in the manuscript draft.

An external validator skill, run after a note is emitted, closes the
loop.

## Requirements

### What the validator does

1. Read a note file at a caller-specified path.
2. Parse the Bibliography section.
3. For each entry: extract DOI and URL; `WebFetch` each; record
   200 vs failure.
4. Parse the Methods section for the "Identifier resolution" line
   that the upstream skill was supposed to write.
5. Compare the validator's results against what the note claims:
   - If the note claims "all N resolved" and the validator confirms,
     write a PASS line to the note's Methods section.
   - If the note claims all resolved but the validator finds
     failures, write a FAIL line and list the failing entries.
   - If the note's resolution line is missing, write a MISSING line
     (the upstream skill misbehaved).

### Output behaviour

- The validator **does not rewrite the note**. It appends a
  validator-provenance line to the Methods section in-place, so the
  author can see both the LLM-side claim and the external check.
- The validator prints a one-line verdict to the caller: `PASS`,
  `FAIL: N entries unresolved`, or `MISSING: no resolution line in
  note`.
- On FAIL, the caller should re-run the upstream skill (or manually
  fix the note) before using its output.

## Non-requirements

- No CI/hook integration. The validator is a manual skill the
  author invokes after each `related-work-note` invocation. Hook
  integration is a separate, harder question.
- No editing of cited-work bodies. The validator only touches the
  Methods section.
- No Crossref metadata fetch. 200 OK is the bar; deeper validation
  is the author's job.

## Actions

1. Draft `~/.claude/skills/related-work-note-validate/SKILL.md`
   (user-level, sibling of the main skill). Accept a note-file path
   as the sole argument.
2. Test on the two pilot notes from ticket 0098
   (`notes/skill-pilot/narrow/` and `notes/skill-pilot/broad/`).
3. Test on one note where a known-bad DOI is inserted by hand —
   validator must FAIL and name the bad entry.
4. Commit the skill. Update the README of the main skill (if any)
   to point at the validator.

## Test

- [ ] Running the validator on a clean pilot note returns `PASS`.
- [ ] Running on a note with a deliberately broken DOI returns
      `FAIL` and names the broken entry.
- [ ] Running on a note whose Methods section omits the
      "Identifier resolution" line returns `MISSING`.
- [ ] The validator never edits cited-work content — only appends
      to Methods.

## Exit criteria

- `~/.claude/skills/related-work-note-validate/SKILL.md` installed.
- Three test cases above pass.
- Operator has reviewed and approved.

## Relationship to other tickets

- **0098** — the main skill. This validator complements it;
  together they provide specify + enforce.
- **0077** — consumer. Once this ticket closes, 0077's workflow
  should invoke the validator after each of its four skill
  invocations.
